        "original_id": "fa303c6c-caeb-56fa-a1bd-9286489ff8af",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sangin, Lashkargah\n- Water bodies: Helmand River, Sistan Basin\n- Concepts: alternate names, watershed\n\nFacts:\n- Sangin is located in the valley of the Helmand River at an altitude of 888 meters.\n- Sangin is 95 kilometers northeast of Lashkargah.\n- The Helmand River is the longest river in Afghanistan.\n- The Helmand River is the primary watershed for the endorheic Sistan Basin.\n- The Helmand River is also spelled Helmend, Helmund, and Hirmand, and it is called Hīrmand or Helmand in Pashto and Persian, Etýmandros in Greek, and Erymandrus in Latin.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
